-- title:
--   Order of the transported local fundamental class in H²(D_w,K_w^×)
-- statement:
--   Let $E \subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$ Galois, and let $w$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $K$. Write $D_w =$ [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) for the decomposition subgroup of $K \simeq_{\text{alg}[E]} K$ attached to the valuation subring of the $w$-adic valuation of $K$, and assume $D_w$ is solvable. Fix a prime $q$ and a finite extension $L'$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\ q$, carrying an action of $D_w$ by semiring automorphisms together with a compatible action on $(L')^\times$, and a ring isomorphism $\Phi \colon K_w \to L'$, where $K_w$ is the $w$-adic completion of $K$. It is assumed that $D_w$ fixes the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in $L'$ pointwise, that the action on $(L')^\times$ is the restriction of the action on $L'$, and that $\Phi$ is $D_w$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a further finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside the same closure which is a base for $L'$ in the sense of [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsBase`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L13), i.e. $K_0 \le L'$ and an element of $L'$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by every element of $D_w$. Let $\theta$ be a morphism of $\mathbb{Z}$-linear $D_w$-representations from the additive copy of $(L')^\times$ to the additive copy of $K_w^\times$ which, on points, is given by $\Phi^{-1}$. Finally let $u \in H^2(D_w, (L')^\times)$ satisfy [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass q L' D_w K₀`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60): for every finite extension $M \ge L'$ inside the closure, every finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$ with normal subgroups $N_L, N_n$, isomorphism $e \colon D_w \cong H/N_L$, element $\varphi \in H$ and unit $\pi$ of $M$ forming an unramified overlayer datum (conditions on fixed fields $K_0 = M^H$, $L' = M^{N_L}$, compatibility of $e$ with the actions, $|H/N_n| = |D_w|$ with $H/N_n$ generated by the image of $\varphi$, a Frobenius congruence for $\varphi$, and normalisation of $\pi$ as a uniformiser of $K_0$, summarised here), and every equivariant map $\iota$ lifting the inclusion $L' \subseteq M$, the pullback of $u$ along $H \to H/N_L \cong D_w$ and $\iota$ is the inflation of the class of the cyclic 'carry' cocycle `carryFun` attached to $\varphi$ and $\pi$. Then for every integer $m$, the $m$-fold multiple of the image of $u$ under the degree-$2$ map induced by the identity of $D_w$ and $\theta$ vanishes in $H^2(D_w, K_w^\times)$ if and only if $|D_w|$ divides $m$.
--
--   This is the local class field theory statement that $H^2(D_w, K_w^\times)$ is cyclic of order $|D_w| = [K_w : E_v]$ with the fundamental class as generator, in the form: the class transported along $\Phi$ has exact additive order $|D_w|$. It is used when a cohomology class has been recognised as a multiple of the fundamental class, to convert divisibility statements about that multiple into vanishing statements, and is cited in the Herbrand-quotient computations and in the construction of the local inverse for ideles.
